		{
			dependencies: [
				"52F1953ED72A8AA6"
				"77582C534A994D7C"
				"27A80F018F59EF1E"
			]
			description: [
				"All of the Tier Four missions require &6Petrotheum Dust&r."
				""
				"This tier of Microminer excels at gathering massive batches of basic materials, such as &6Iron&r, &6Gold&r, or &6Redstone&r. Additionally, this microminer will be your first source of &6Neptunium&r."
				""
				"It is also a convenient source of &6Sheldonite&r, the best choice for creating &6Platinum Group Sludge&r, via a mission requiring &6Wither Realm Data&r."
			]
			id: "15DBB22E3DC0AFB7"
			rewards: [{
				id: "48E752C131EA99AC"
				item: "kubejs:moni_quarter"
				type: "item"
			}]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 2.0d
			tasks: [{
				id: "41398E76BAF0F92E"
				item: "kubejs:microminer_t4"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Tier Four Microminer"
			x: 13.25d
			y: 4.75d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["53C00EA9D9BEE776"]
			description: [
				"&6Indium&r is a rare material requiring specialized bulk ore processing to acquire. It is useful for making &6Indium Gallium Phosphide&r (InGaP)."
				""
				"You will need to purify (with an &3Ore Washer&r or &3Chemical Bath&r) &6Galena&r and &6Sphalerite&r to get &6Purified&r crushed ore. These need to be placed together in a &3Mixer&r along with &9Sulfuric Acid&r, which will result in &9Indium Concentrate&r."
				""
				"This in turn needs to be reacted with &6Aluminium&r in a &3Chemical Reactor&r, to create &2Small Piles of Indium Dust, Aluminium Sulfite and &9Lead-Zinc Solution&r. The latter two can be centrifuged into various useful materials, and the Indium piles can be combined into full dusts."
				""
				"Later on, you can substitute &6Argentite&r for &6Galena&r or &6Sphalerite&r. &2Indium can also be obtained from the Naquadah processing chain in LuV."
			]
			id: "6E5343E45E99CBAD"
			rewards: [{
				id: "6655983AB054E8EA"
				item: "kubejs:moni_nickel"
				type: "item"
			}]
			shape: "hexagon"
			tasks: [{
				id: "76BD7DC9E8DFF0C6"
				item: "gtceu:indium_dust"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Indium"
			x: -4.5d
			y: -4.75d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"6E5343E45E99CBAD"
				"11154356854B64DA"
			]
			dependency_requirement: "one_completed"
			description: [
				"&6QBit CPUs&r are an advanced Circuit Wafer crucial for &6Quantum Circuits&r."
				""
				"There are two methods of creating them:"
				""
				"The simpler recipe uses two &6Quantum Eyes&r and two ingots' worth of molten &9Gallium Arsenide&r to enhance a &6NanoCPU Wafer&r. This recipe is slow and requires substantially more &9Radon&r per craft."
				""
				"The other route instead uses &6Indium Gallium Phosphide&r and a tiny amount of Radon. This skips the slow-crafting Quantum Eyes, using far less Radon in the process, but requires the infrastructure in place for obtaining &6Indium&r."
				""
				"The second route is overall better, and you will need Indium processing to complete the pack so might as well do it."
			]
			id: "1903B26C95DD325A"
			rewards: [{
				id: "6AC4AD3CD3FE51B3"
				item: "kubejs:moni_nickel"
				type: "item"
			}]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{
				id: "1A7AA84791A76177"
				item: "gtceu:qbit_cpu_chip"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "QBit Processing Unit"
			x: -4.5d
			y: -6.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"672D43BD113251EA"
				"605062720747B482"
			]
			description: [
				"The &3Assembly Line&r is a large multiblock structure that crafts complex materials, similar to an &3Assembler&r. These will be crucial going forward for making a variety of components and machinery."
				""
				"Make sure your power generation and circuit production are up to the challenge. &2None of the Assembly Line recipes require programmed circuits.&r"
				""
				"This quest calls for an Assembly Line that's 10 units long, allowing for 9 inputs and one output. This is a large enough Assembly Line to make &6LuV components&r, but you'll need to expand to more inputs for later projects."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"The structure of the Assembly Line is a little stricter than other multiblocks:"
				""
				"- The &aInput Buses&r can only be placed along the bottom, must all be &8ULV&r tier, and must face downwards. The &aOutput Bus&r must be placed at the very end of the row of Input Buses, and can be any tier."
				""
				"- &aFluid Hatches&r can only replace the &6Steel Casings&r along the bottom."
				""
				"- &aEnergy Hatches&r can only be placed within the top row of &6Steel Casings&r."
				""
				"- The &2Data Access Hatch&r must replace a &6Grate Casing&r on the same side as the Assembly Line controller block. Later, you can replace this with an &2Optical Data Reception Hatch&r. Refer to adjacent quests for how the Assembly Line data system works."
				""
				"If your recipe is not running, ensure you have the corresponding &edata&r for the recipe in a &2Data Access Hatch&r or connected &3Data Bank&r."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:assembly_line"
