		{
			dependencies: ["39FD6F1076559156"]
			description: [
				"The &3Assembly Line&r needs to be provided with &edata&r on how to craft items before it can craft them. Data on how to craft each item is stored in a &6Data Stick&r and read by a &aData Access Hatch&r. This data is required to craft &6LuV components&r and the &3Fusion Reactor&r, among other things."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"To begin, craft a &3Scanner&r and a few &6Data Sticks&r. The initial Scanner recipes run at &6HV&r, but &9IV&r is required relatively soon so might as well make that one."
				""
				"Press &8R&r on the item you want to craft in &bEMI&r and navigate to the &bScanner tab&r. This will tell you which item needs to be scanned to make the data for the new item. For example, &dLuV &6Electric Motors&r will require an &9IV&r &6Electric Motor&r to be scanned."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Place a &6Data Stick&r with the item to be scanned in the &3Scanner&r. The item will be &cconsumed&r and its data will be written to the &6Data Stick&r. Each &6Data item&r can only hold a &csingle recipe&r."
				""
				"Finally, place the &6Data Stick&r into the &aData Access Hatch&r of your &3Assembly Line&r. It will now be able to craft that item."
				""
				"Later, you will need more advanced &6Data Orbs&r and &6Data Modules&r to store data, and a &3Data Bank&r to read them."
				""
				"If you need to create duplicate Data items, you can copy the data to a blank data item of the same type using the Scanner."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:data_stick"
			id: "672D43BD113251EA"
